WEBVTT

00:04.627 --> 00:07.880
[crowd chattering]

00:07.963 --> 00:09.006
[child laughs]

00:09.089 --> 00:10.925
-Quick.
-[mother] Okay.

00:11.008 --> 00:12.009
SAFE WATER

00:12.092 --> 00:13.010
MORNING STAR GRAPH
NEWSPAPER

00:13.093 --> 00:14.011
Get your newspapers!

00:14.094 --> 00:16.388
MOVIES

00:16.472 --> 00:20.059
We can take two more resource collectors!

00:20.142 --> 00:21.644
Let me join, will ya?

00:21.727 --> 00:23.687
MUSIC SWAP SHOP - OPEN

00:23.771 --> 00:25.689
Oh! <i>GAGA</i> by Peat Moth.

00:26.732 --> 00:29.235
You found a rare one.

00:29.318 --> 00:32.488
If it still plays,
it's worth four hundred thousand.

00:32.571 --> 00:34.657
[gasps] No way!

00:36.909 --> 00:38.702
[huffs]

00:43.999 --> 00:46.835
-Oh, man! I really wanted to hear it!
-[cries]

00:46.919 --> 00:47.920
[chuckles]

00:48.003 --> 00:50.297
[video game music playing]

00:52.258 --> 00:54.551
Sis still isn't done yet?

00:54.635 --> 00:56.762
MARU - KIRUKO

00:56.845 --> 00:59.348
[video game battle music playing]

00:59.431 --> 01:01.225
LOOK OUT, MONSTERS!

01:03.560 --> 01:05.688
-[chuckles] What have we here?
-[thugs laugh]

01:05.771 --> 01:08.232
Crocodile Quest, right?

01:08.315 --> 01:11.193
Why are you only using two people,
when you could use four?

01:11.777 --> 01:14.113
-[laughs]
-Not from around here, are ya?

01:14.196 --> 01:18.200
If you're gonna play here,
you better speak when spoken to.

01:18.284 --> 01:19.285
Hi.

01:20.035 --> 01:23.455
Ever had a girl you like
turn out to be a guy? Can you imagine?

01:23.539 --> 01:26.375
-Can't say I've come across that--
-[gasps]

01:27.084 --> 01:30.004
What's that got to do with anything?

01:30.879 --> 01:35.592
-[gasps]
-Don't just say "Hi." Insolent brat!

01:36.302 --> 01:37.594
[sighs]

01:37.678 --> 01:39.513
[grunts, groans]

01:40.389 --> 01:42.016
[groans]

01:42.099 --> 01:44.018
-Hey.
-[thugs gasp]

01:44.101 --> 01:46.687
-Wasn't one whack enough?
-[thug 1 groaning]

01:47.187 --> 01:50.149
What was the kick for? Say sorry!

01:50.983 --> 01:52.192
Guess you're right.

01:52.276 --> 01:54.194
[groaning continues]

01:54.278 --> 01:55.612
Sorry.

01:56.363 --> 01:57.823
[grunts, coughs]

01:57.906 --> 01:59.033
[chuckles]

01:59.533 --> 02:02.703
Take it outside, will you?
You're tearing the place up.

02:02.786 --> 02:05.205
[groans] Ouch.

02:05.289 --> 02:07.291
Oops, look at you now.

02:07.374 --> 02:10.336
Why you looking away
in the middle of fight?

02:10.419 --> 02:12.671
[thug 2] Is he stupid or, what? Moron.

02:12.755 --> 02:14.590
[thugs laughing]

02:16.759 --> 02:18.510
[laughs]

02:25.225 --> 02:28.020
[thugs grunting, groaning]

02:28.729 --> 02:30.564
Wait, stop.

02:31.440 --> 02:32.441
You brat!

02:33.734 --> 02:34.985
[grunts]

02:36.695 --> 02:39.114
What the hell is this guy?

02:41.492 --> 02:43.077
[screams]

02:44.244 --> 02:45.371
[grunts, groans]

02:49.375 --> 02:50.376
[Kiruko grunts]

02:50.459 --> 02:53.212
-Sis?
-Are you okay, Maru?

02:53.295 --> 02:57.549
Whoa, why did you bulldoze in
with no clue what's going on?

02:57.633 --> 02:59.593
What if it was my fault?

03:00.177 --> 03:02.096
We've been hanging out for ages.

03:02.179 --> 03:05.349
I think I'd know if you were the type
who looks for fights.

03:06.642 --> 03:10.104
And anyway,
who knows if he was about to call backup.

03:10.187 --> 03:12.064
If you attack, you've got to get them all.

03:12.147 --> 03:14.233
-Guess so.
-It's not just "Guess so."

03:14.316 --> 03:16.193
Wait, your tooth!

03:16.276 --> 03:18.195
-Your tooth broke off.
-[sighs]

03:19.113 --> 03:20.197
Hey, let me see.

03:20.781 --> 03:22.408
It'll grow back.

03:22.491 --> 03:24.618
It won't grow back. It's an adult tooth!

03:25.744 --> 03:26.870
Let's get out of here.

03:27.371 --> 03:29.540
Let's get further away
then sleep somewhere.

05:05.844 --> 05:09.473
[Maru] <i>I was born the same year
as the Great Disaster, apparently.</i>

05:11.558 --> 05:15.229
<i>The first memories I have
are from three or four years old.</i>

05:16.438 --> 05:20.484
<i>I lived in a spacious room
with other kids about my age.</i>

05:21.610 --> 05:23.237
<i>I was cold and hungry,</i>

05:23.737 --> 05:27.866
<i>but there were adults to take care of me,
so it wasn't so bad.</i>

05:29.618 --> 05:32.996
<i>I think I was about seven
when the place closed down, I guess.</i>

05:33.747 --> 05:36.542
<i>The adults took us all
to different locations.</i>

05:37.876 --> 05:39.503
<i>There were others like me,</i>

05:40.087 --> 05:41.797
<i>without any relatives, I suppose.</i>

05:42.297 --> 05:44.383
<i>We were all put in a separate group</i>

05:44.466 --> 05:47.803
<i>and somehow
survived on scraps for three years.</i>

05:48.428 --> 05:52.849
<i>The adult who led our group,
was killed over some sort of turf war.</i>

05:53.475 --> 05:56.019
<i>We went with the killer,</i>

05:56.812 --> 05:59.147
<i>and became part of their gang.</i>

05:59.690 --> 06:01.733
<i>I was still working with them
until recently.</i>

06:05.112 --> 06:08.865
<i>Then Mikura turned up and took me in.</i>

06:10.450 --> 06:14.746
<i>She was the one who taught me
how to kill Hiruko.</i>

06:14.830 --> 06:15.831
DAY OF FATE

06:15.914 --> 06:19.668
Did you think of Mikura as a woman?

06:19.751 --> 06:20.919
Huh?

06:21.503 --> 06:22.504
Not really.

06:23.005 --> 06:26.091
She was just the next person
I had to listen to.

06:26.592 --> 06:27.593
Hmm.

06:28.176 --> 06:30.137
You don't fall in love easily, then?

06:30.220 --> 06:31.680
[Maru] What are you talking about?

06:32.180 --> 06:36.476
Anyway, whenever she looked at me,
she always had this coldness in her eyes.

06:36.977 --> 06:38.854
She didn't really treat me like a human.

06:40.439 --> 06:45.152
Can't you at least remember
where the town is, or the name of it?

06:45.777 --> 06:48.280
Until I started traveling with Mikura,

06:48.363 --> 06:50.824
I didn't know how big Japan was.

06:50.907 --> 06:56.038
I didn't even have any idea
where I was in Japan.

06:56.705 --> 07:00.292
My life has basically consisted
of nothing but following adults around.

07:00.375 --> 07:01.376
Don't be dramatic.

07:02.669 --> 07:05.005
Especially if you're not offering
any new information.

07:05.088 --> 07:07.758
I've told you the story a thousand times.
What did you expect?

07:07.841 --> 07:10.010
Not the point.
If you tell it over and over,

07:10.093 --> 07:13.096
you might remember something,
or notice something.

07:14.306 --> 07:15.766
I read that somewhere.

07:15.849 --> 07:18.894
Oh, yeah. Speaking of books,
have you seen the next room?

07:18.977 --> 07:21.688
There are so many books! Let's sell them.

07:21.772 --> 07:25.692
I packed as many novels and comics
as I could while you were sleeping.

07:26.693 --> 07:30.530
I'm going to burn any books
that seem useful after I've read them.

07:31.114 --> 07:35.661
Knowledge has more value
if you keep it to yourself.

07:35.744 --> 07:36.912
[Maru] Oh, got it.

07:36.995 --> 07:38.205
MORNING STAR GRAPH NO. 336

07:38.288 --> 07:40.540
Oh, that's a newspaper from the town.

07:41.124 --> 07:42.793
Why don't you read it while waiting?

07:42.876 --> 07:45.545
Aren't we going shopping together?

07:45.629 --> 07:47.798
Your face will get us busted.

07:47.881 --> 07:51.009
We'll be in a total mess
if the guys from yesterday recognize you.

07:51.093 --> 07:52.094
Hmm?

07:52.928 --> 07:54.638
[groans]

07:56.181 --> 07:57.182
It's fine!

07:57.265 --> 07:58.892
It's a bit swollen, but it's not busted.

07:58.975 --> 08:00.644
[groans]

08:00.727 --> 08:02.020
Oh boy.

08:02.646 --> 08:04.106
Try to understand, okay?

08:04.189 --> 08:06.942
I'm not saying your face is busted.

08:07.025 --> 08:09.194
I'm saying your face will get us busted.

08:11.988 --> 08:15.742
So, if Mikura taught you everything,

08:15.826 --> 08:17.828
does that mean she has the Maru-Touch too?

08:17.911 --> 08:20.539
No, she said only I could do it.

08:21.206 --> 08:23.792
And that's why I need to go to Heaven.

08:25.001 --> 08:29.214
By the way, the poster at your office
said you could kill Man-eaters.

08:29.798 --> 08:31.758
That was just advertising.

08:36.430 --> 08:38.515
CHARGING SHOP

08:38.598 --> 08:39.933
TRADING AVAILABLE

08:41.017 --> 08:44.980
Where'd he disappear to?
The stupid kid with the disheveled hair.

08:45.647 --> 08:48.275
That brat doesn't bother me.

08:48.358 --> 08:50.861
We should be focusing
on the Ministry of Reconstruction.

08:50.944 --> 08:52.738
[thug 1] You think they're nearby?

08:52.821 --> 08:55.741
[thug 2] No idea.
That rumor is always flying about.

08:56.491 --> 08:58.160
[Kiruko] <i>Ministry of Reconstruction.</i>

08:58.243 --> 09:00.370
<i>That rumor is still being passed around?</i>

09:02.664 --> 09:05.667
[Robin] There's a group abducting people
with the right skills and expertise

09:06.251 --> 09:09.796
to get civilization back to how it was.

09:09.880 --> 09:11.965
-[gasps]
-Are they going to come to Asakusa?

09:12.048 --> 09:13.049
[chuckles]

09:13.133 --> 09:15.677
It's just a rumor, but they might.

09:15.761 --> 09:19.347
Sis said that's just a fantasy
that old people believe.

09:19.431 --> 09:21.224
That's an alternative explanation.

09:21.308 --> 09:22.642
Wait a sec.

09:22.726 --> 09:26.897
Does this have something to do
with all those disappearances?

09:26.980 --> 09:31.276
Well, you guys have pretty special skills
fixing all those electro-karts.

09:31.985 --> 09:35.322
Better to act stupid
if someone you don't know comes along.

09:35.947 --> 09:38.533
How would you act stupid? Ran?

09:38.617 --> 09:39.743
Huh?

09:39.826 --> 09:41.453
Oh, you're good at it.

09:41.536 --> 09:43.288
I didn't do anything yet!

09:43.371 --> 09:45.499
[laughing]

09:46.541 --> 09:47.542
[chuckles]

09:47.626 --> 09:49.419
WATER SAFETY LEVEL 80%

09:49.503 --> 09:53.840
We've searched all over the place
and he's not here. Must have left.

09:54.382 --> 09:56.927
But what if he's still here?

09:57.010 --> 09:59.304
We'll just grab him.

09:59.387 --> 10:02.474
Iwata said he wants another round.
One on one.

10:02.557 --> 10:06.186
You wouldn't say that
if you were there yesterday.

10:06.269 --> 10:09.856
There were eight of us
and he completely destroyed us.

10:10.440 --> 10:12.234
He's like an explosive.

10:12.317 --> 10:13.860
No way I want a second round.

10:14.861 --> 10:15.862
[chuckles]

10:15.946 --> 10:17.697
My little Maru is strong, huh?

10:21.618 --> 10:23.328
My Maru?

10:25.539 --> 10:27.874
Why am I proud of him?

10:29.835 --> 10:32.087
<i>I'm just his bodyguard.</i>

10:32.671 --> 10:36.174
<i>Once he finds what he's looking for,
I'll be alone again.</i>

10:41.555 --> 10:42.806
[gasps]

10:44.724 --> 10:45.725
What…

10:47.686 --> 10:48.687
Maru?

10:53.817 --> 10:54.860
Hey, Maru.

10:55.944 --> 10:57.362
[gasps]

10:57.445 --> 10:59.573
[wind howling]

11:01.324 --> 11:02.492
MORNING STAR GRAPH

11:05.245 --> 11:06.329
[gasps]

11:07.289 --> 11:08.832
Ma-- Maru!

11:08.915 --> 11:11.251
[heavy breathing]

11:11.334 --> 11:12.586
Maru!

11:14.170 --> 11:15.297
[whimpers]

11:16.798 --> 11:17.799
Maru.

11:17.883 --> 11:19.759
[whimpers]

11:19.843 --> 11:21.761
Where is he?

11:22.262 --> 11:24.222
-[Kiruko gasps]
-Be quiet!

11:24.306 --> 11:26.099
Why are you yelling like that?

11:26.182 --> 11:28.560
-I was hiding like I'm meant to be.
-[sighs]

11:30.145 --> 11:33.440
What were you doing in the next room?

11:34.024 --> 11:37.319
What? I was just…

11:37.986 --> 11:41.031
I was looking to see
if there are any useful books in there.

11:41.114 --> 11:43.617
[groans] Hey, wait!
There's nothing to see.

11:43.700 --> 11:45.410
YOUNG LADY'S SPECIAL LESSON

11:46.661 --> 11:47.913
[Kiruko] I get it.

11:47.996 --> 11:49.998
You were just using those porno magazines.

11:50.081 --> 11:52.292
[Maru] Using? I was just look--

11:52.375 --> 11:54.252
Wait, I wasn't looking either!

11:55.754 --> 11:58.590
Sis! What happened?

11:58.673 --> 11:59.674
You seem weird.

12:01.009 --> 12:04.220
I never thought I would panic like that.

12:04.930 --> 12:09.142
I got back and you weren't here.
Please don't do that again.

12:09.643 --> 12:11.144
I told you before.

12:11.811 --> 12:14.230
I might not always
be exactly where you left me.

12:14.314 --> 12:15.607
-[crying]
-[gasps]

12:18.234 --> 12:20.111
-[gasps]
-[crying continues]

12:21.279 --> 12:23.782
Sorry, I was wrong.

12:24.282 --> 12:26.284
I think?

12:27.702 --> 12:31.831
When I was telling you
about my upbringing,

12:33.124 --> 12:37.170
I was wondering
whether yours had been even worse.

12:40.382 --> 12:41.591
Hey.

12:42.258 --> 12:45.679
I-- I can feel something hard.

12:45.762 --> 12:47.055
[grunts]

12:47.138 --> 12:49.599
You can't blame me!
I was already halfway--

12:49.683 --> 12:52.185
Wait, I wasn't halfway anywhere…

12:52.268 --> 12:53.436
-[chuckles]
-…but even so!

12:56.940 --> 12:59.776
[Maru] I was reading something
in the newspaper.

12:59.859 --> 13:04.030
Before the Great Disaster,
humans made robots to make life easier.

13:04.656 --> 13:08.868
But they started to get nervous
that the robots were monitoring them.

13:08.952 --> 13:10.078
[laughs]

13:10.161 --> 13:11.371
[Maru] But the truth is,

13:11.454 --> 13:15.750
humans had too much spare time,
and ended up monitoring each other.

13:15.834 --> 13:17.877
They started to push their own rules
onto each other,

13:18.461 --> 13:20.964
and slaughtered one another
until everything perished.

13:21.464 --> 13:23.883
[Kiruko] That's the War Collapse Theory.

13:23.967 --> 13:25.552
Sounds made up to me.

13:25.635 --> 13:27.554
It's too much like an old fable.

13:27.637 --> 13:30.724
The story just means that life before
wasn't just like Heaven.

13:31.224 --> 13:34.102
Besides, if Heaven existed
before the Great Disaster,

13:34.185 --> 13:37.981
I'd have to go into the past,
which is impossible.

13:38.064 --> 13:42.986
But everyone who knows about life before,
wants to go back.

13:43.778 --> 13:44.904
What if,

13:45.613 --> 13:49.451
somewhere out there,
civilization has already been restored?

13:52.287 --> 13:53.997
[computer beeping]

13:56.624 --> 13:57.917
Hmm?

14:00.837 --> 14:01.838
Hmm?

14:04.132 --> 14:05.216
Is that…

14:07.343 --> 14:08.344
a footprint?

14:10.263 --> 14:13.475
Why would there be a footprint here?

14:15.602 --> 14:16.978
[folk music playing]

14:20.148 --> 14:21.566
[bells jingle]

14:40.001 --> 14:41.086
What are you doing?

14:41.169 --> 14:44.547
If Tarao hears some fun sounds,
he might wake up.

14:44.631 --> 14:45.924
[Taka grunting]

14:48.343 --> 14:49.594
And over there?

14:49.677 --> 14:52.597
When Tarao was well,
apparently he could pick up that rock.

14:53.181 --> 14:54.974
He didn't just pick it up.

14:55.058 --> 14:57.227
He could throw it all the way over there.

14:58.353 --> 15:00.313
Tarao was really strong.

15:00.939 --> 15:04.526
[Taka grunts] I can do it too!

15:05.902 --> 15:08.321
-[folk music ends]
-[rhythmic beeping]

15:10.907 --> 15:12.784
[steady beep]

15:13.868 --> 15:19.374
[doctor] Ten'ei 17, October 16th,
11:34 p.m.

15:21.376 --> 15:22.377
I'm so sorry.

15:24.129 --> 15:25.839
[cries]

15:28.925 --> 15:30.885
[robot teacher] <i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

15:31.386 --> 15:33.054
-<i>Once dressed…
</i>-[yawns]

15:33.138 --> 15:35.974
<i>…please come to the square
before going to breakfast.</i>

15:37.475 --> 15:40.270
<i>Tarao passed away last night.</i>

15:40.353 --> 15:41.354
[gasps]

15:43.231 --> 15:44.482
[whimpers]

15:44.566 --> 15:48.236
[cries]

15:51.072 --> 15:53.992
[Kuku crying]

16:00.415 --> 16:02.417
[crying continues]

16:27.942 --> 16:30.278
Did Asura have the same disease?

16:30.361 --> 16:31.404
[gasps]

16:34.908 --> 16:36.034
Asura…

16:39.621 --> 16:40.872
Yeah.

16:41.915 --> 16:43.917
Maybe, yes.

16:47.795 --> 16:52.008
Mina, may we cremate Tarao's body?

16:52.091 --> 16:56.304
<i>Yes, we've already taken
the samples we need.</i>

16:57.096 --> 16:59.432
It's desperately sad.

17:00.266 --> 17:04.437
This is the second death
among the children.

17:04.520 --> 17:08.107
No one could have predicted
Asura's suicide.

17:08.191 --> 17:09.192
-That's not true.
-[gasps]

17:09.817 --> 17:13.529
Asura was born into a body
that could not bear its own mind.

17:14.030 --> 17:15.156
ASURA - TEN'EI 12, MAY 7TH

17:15.240 --> 17:17.867
We are the ones responsible
for Asura's death.

17:19.035 --> 17:22.038
Too many cruel ideas
were forced upon Asura.

17:22.538 --> 17:25.959
Asura's birth itself was a sin.

17:26.626 --> 17:30.213
Put Tarao's grave next to Asura's.

17:34.550 --> 17:38.972
Was Tarao's illness a strange one? Or…

17:39.639 --> 17:43.935
If an illness developed within a body
built with immunity to everything,

17:44.018 --> 17:46.938
then it's possible that all the children
could fall ill.

17:47.021 --> 17:49.065
[Director] Then we have a big problem!

17:49.148 --> 17:51.734
The Day of Fate is the only thing
that can't be changed.

17:51.818 --> 17:56.072
Until then,
figure out what it is and how to cure it!

17:56.823 --> 17:59.492
[retching]

17:59.575 --> 18:01.828
[coughs]

18:04.497 --> 18:05.748
[Tokio] Me too?

18:06.666 --> 18:08.835
Am I sick too?

18:10.795 --> 18:11.838
[Kiruko] What do you think?

18:11.921 --> 18:16.092
I sold all the books in my backpack
and bought this map.

18:16.676 --> 18:18.678
That's the value of information.

18:18.761 --> 18:21.431
Yeah, right.

18:22.056 --> 18:24.684
"Water safety level, 50%."

18:25.852 --> 18:28.062
What are these numbers based on?

18:28.146 --> 18:31.441
The guy at the map store said it's
based on taste and how clear it looks.

18:31.524 --> 18:33.276
That's subjective, isn't it?

18:34.986 --> 18:37.822
"Water safety level, 100%."

18:37.905 --> 18:38.990
100%?

18:39.073 --> 18:43.119
A place where the water is
100% safe would be Heaven, right?

18:43.202 --> 18:44.662
That's subjective.

18:45.455 --> 18:48.499
-I guess we could stop by, though.
-[footsteps approaching]

18:48.583 --> 18:49.667
[gasps]

18:50.251 --> 18:51.961
Quiet! I hear footsteps.

18:54.464 --> 18:56.632
Someone's in the building.

18:57.133 --> 18:59.135
[footsteps continue]

19:01.179 --> 19:02.388
-[knocks]
-[gasps]

19:02.472 --> 19:04.474
They're coming straight for us.

19:04.557 --> 19:06.476
Do you think that gang has found us?

19:07.268 --> 19:10.646
Sounds like just one guy.
We can probably handle it if we need to.

19:10.730 --> 19:13.775
What are you gonna do if he's mega strong?

19:13.858 --> 19:15.318
-[stranger] I know you're in there!
-[gasps]

19:16.069 --> 19:18.488
[stranger] I was on the ship with you.
Let me in.

19:21.115 --> 19:24.911
I spotted you in the tent city
and followed you here.

19:25.495 --> 19:27.663
I'll get straight to the point.

19:28.373 --> 19:30.291
Will you protect me?

19:30.375 --> 19:33.836
Well, if we're heading the same way,
I'll think about it.

19:34.337 --> 19:36.047
I'm not going too far.

19:36.130 --> 19:37.298
Just to the Immortal Order.

19:37.882 --> 19:40.009
-Immortal Order?
-What's that?

19:40.093 --> 19:42.970
Well, at least, that's what it's called.

19:43.054 --> 19:45.640
But maybe it has a different name.

19:46.432 --> 19:49.769
I heard there is a doctor
who can keep you alive forever.

19:49.852 --> 19:52.021
A doctor. A doctor?

19:52.522 --> 19:54.440
The doctor, is it this man?

19:55.775 --> 19:58.986
Wait. I haven't been there, or met him.

19:59.070 --> 20:00.196
Where is it?

20:00.780 --> 20:02.073
[groans]

20:02.698 --> 20:05.201
If you don't tell me,
I won't be your bodyguard.

20:05.284 --> 20:07.495
I can't take on the job
if you don't trust me.

20:08.871 --> 20:11.207
I've trusted you since
I saw what you did on the ship.

20:12.500 --> 20:15.711
I need you to protect me,
and the contents of this bag.

20:15.795 --> 20:18.131
Those things that appeared
after the Great Disaster,

20:18.214 --> 20:21.050
like that indestructible monstrosity
that attacked the ship--

20:21.551 --> 20:23.845
If you transplant part of a monster
onto a human,

20:23.928 --> 20:26.556
they become extremely powerful
and have immortal life.

20:26.639 --> 20:28.349
Had you heard that before?

20:28.433 --> 20:32.353
Don't tell me that bag you're carrying…

20:32.437 --> 20:34.313
[laughs]

20:34.397 --> 20:35.606
Don't take it from me.

20:36.357 --> 20:37.817
Don't dare take it.

20:40.903 --> 20:42.155
Uh…

20:42.238 --> 20:45.116
Isn't it rotting? It's all sloppy.

20:45.199 --> 20:47.326
Huh? What? [gasps]

20:47.910 --> 20:50.830
It wasn't like this
before I got on the ship.

20:51.664 --> 20:52.915
Don't chuck it everywhere!

20:52.999 --> 20:55.668
[stranger whimpers]

20:56.502 --> 20:57.503
Why?

20:58.629 --> 21:01.007
After I finally got my hands on it.

21:01.090 --> 21:02.425
[crying]

21:04.427 --> 21:05.428
Hey, pops.

21:05.511 --> 21:07.930
Where is this Indestructible Order,
or whatever?

21:08.014 --> 21:09.974
-Wasn't it the Immortal Order?
-[crying continues]

21:11.017 --> 21:13.394
I'll buy the information from you.

21:14.395 --> 21:17.732
You can use the money
to find more Man-eater parts.

21:17.815 --> 21:19.442
[stranger cries]

21:22.278 --> 21:25.490
Let's get some of that 100% safe water,
then off to the Immortal Order.

21:25.573 --> 21:27.825
Sorry, it's a bit of a detour.

21:27.909 --> 21:29.494
[Maru] Doesn't matter to me.

21:30.244 --> 21:33.498
There's a chance the Immortal Order
could be where Heaven is too.

21:34.081 --> 21:37.251
But, there's something a bit dodgy
about the location.

21:37.835 --> 21:40.963
On the map, it just says "strange people."

21:41.047 --> 21:42.256
STRANGE PEOPLE RESIDE HERE

21:43.049 --> 21:44.342
-[footsteps approach]
-[knocking]

21:44.926 --> 21:46.344
Director! It's urgent!

21:46.427 --> 21:48.304
Why are you crashing about like that?

21:48.387 --> 21:50.515
Tarao has been cremated, but--

21:50.598 --> 21:52.808
[Director] Deal with the rest yourself.

21:52.892 --> 21:54.810
-But you need to see this!
-[screams]

21:57.021 --> 21:58.439
[screams]

21:58.523 --> 21:59.857
[grunts]

21:59.941 --> 22:01.984
What on earth is going on?

22:02.693 --> 22:03.778
[gasps]

22:08.658 --> 22:09.951
[gasps]

22:10.660 --> 22:12.495
[Director] What is it?
